    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0881" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-07T13:00:00+09:00">January 7, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 7—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Embassy’s 246, December 19, 3 p.m.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d786-f1"/> I
                    discussed the situation of the oil companies today with the Vice Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs<anchor n="65" xml:id="d786-f2"/> on the basis of paragraph 4 of
                    Embassy’s 240 December 13, 6 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d786-f3"/> The Vice
                    Minister made no comment except to say that the Government had no intention to
                    deprive the foreign companies of a reasonable economic return and that he would
                    see what if anything could be done.</p>
                <p>The Dutch Minister recently made similar representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
